  "suite_sha256": "2aed5018a41f5e08a4d2fd534cb95e6ac1344a91b414689be301dc5b8e0543ef",
  "rationale": "Prior suites explored basic success paths, repeated releases, and simple type violations. This batch addresses previously untested contract clauses and boundaries: (1) float types, string types, and upper-bound out-of-range quantities (qty > 10 is invalid, distinct from insufficient stock); (2) explicit contract clause stating extra fields are ignored on all operations; (3) key payload binding conflict persisting even after key release; (4) releasing keys that failed due to insufficient stock or invalid quantity returns not_found; (5) tenant isolation and stock query verification on completely fresh tenants before any reservations; (6) key identity verification against whitespace padding and shared prefix collisions without truncation; (7) stock operation validation enforcing exact sku case ('WIDGET' vs 'widget') and empty tenant strings; and (8) interleaved multi-sku full consumption and replenishment lifecycles.",
  "origin": "live Google DeepMind / Gemini; fresh context, implementation withheld"
}